1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,960
Nvidia lost around a hundred and ninety
billion dollars of market value on Monday.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,584
But the question investors are asking
goes beyond the price of a chip.

3
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:13,064
Its founder and chief
executive, Jensen Huang,

4
00:00:13,104 --> 00:00:15,968
has admitted being unfaithful to his wife.

5
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:20,736
Nvidia's board has opened an independent
investigation following reports of a

6
00:00:20,776 --> 00:00:23,337
foreign intelligence effort targeting him.

7
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:25,021
And Washington wants answers.

8
00:00:26,361 --> 00:00:29,595
There are two dates to watch:
earnings on November seventeenth,

9
00:00:29,635 --> 00:00:32,766
and a congressional briefing
requested for the following day.

10
00:00:32,806 --> 00:00:34,234
They test very different things.

11
00:00:35,574 --> 00:00:40,418
By the end of this video, you'll know
what is confirmed, what remains alleged,

12
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:43,611
and what could actually
change the investment case.

13
00:00:43,651 --> 00:00:45,808
This is AI Finance Toolkit.

14
00:00:45,848 --> 00:00:49,016
Our research snapshot is the
morning of November tenth.

15
00:00:53,656 --> 00:00:55,030
Start with the sequence,

16
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:59,450
because it is easy to mix separate
developments into one dramatic headline.

17
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:03,132
In late October, the New York
Times reported on Alice Huang,

18
00:01:03,172 --> 00:01:06,078
a former executive at
Singapore-based Megaspeed.

19
00:01:06,118 --> 00:01:10,425
The newspaper reported that US
intelligence had assessed her as a Chinese

20
00:01:10,465 --> 00:01:14,415
intelligence asset and examined
her relationship with Jensen Huang.

21
00:01:14,455 --> 00:01:18,099
That is attributed reporting
about an intelligence assessment.

22
00:01:18,139 --> 00:01:21,640
We cannot independently establish
the underlying intelligence.

23
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:27,292
On November eighth, Jensen published
a message to Nvidia employees.

24
00:01:27,332 --> 00:01:31,885
One sentence was unambiguous:
“I was unfaithful to my wife.”

25
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:34,719
His public email did not
name the other person.

26
00:01:36,059 --> 00:01:39,438
The board separately announced
an independent investigation,

27
00:01:39,478 --> 00:01:42,572
overseen by independent
directors with outside counsel.

28
00:01:42,612 --> 00:01:45,791
It said it had no reason to
believe that national security

29
00:01:45,831 --> 00:01:49,953
or company secrets had been compromised,
and expressed confidence in Jensen

30
00:01:49,993 --> 00:01:51,285
and the leadership team.

31
00:01:52,625 --> 00:01:54,604
Keep those distinctions in view.

32
00:01:54,644 --> 00:01:59,600
An admission about personal conduct does
not establish every allegation surrounding

33
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,040
it.

34
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:04,930
Equally, a board expressing confidence does
not mean its investigation is finished.

35
00:02:04,970 --> 00:02:09,768
China's foreign ministry has rejected
the espionage allegations as groundless.

36
00:02:09,808 --> 00:02:11,994
That denial belongs in the account too.

37
00:02:16,234 --> 00:02:18,704
Why does this become a stock-market story?

38
00:02:18,744 --> 00:02:20,316
Here is our analysis.

39
00:02:20,356 --> 00:02:21,871
First, leadership.

40
00:02:21,911 --> 00:02:26,309
A founder can be central to customer
relationships, product direction

41
00:02:26,349 --> 00:02:27,852
and investor confidence.

42
00:02:27,892 --> 00:02:31,885
Uncertainty around that person can
create uncertainty around the company,

43
00:02:31,925 --> 00:02:35,807
even before there is evidence that
customers have changed their orders.

44
00:02:35,847 --> 00:02:38,430
That is leadership concentration risk.

45
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,341
It does not mean Jensen is leaving.

46
00:02:40,381 --> 00:02:43,430
The board's published position
supports his leadership.

47
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:47,304
But investors can still ask
how decisions, responsibilities

48
00:02:47,344 --> 00:02:50,652
and continuity would work
if circumstances changed.

49
00:02:51,992 --> 00:02:53,573
Second, policy.

50
00:02:53,613 --> 00:02:58,235
Nvidia sits inside a highly sensitive
debate about access to advanced computing.

51
00:02:58,275 --> 00:03:02,468
If lawmakers respond with tighter
export rules, security requirements

52
00:03:02,508 --> 00:03:04,431
or closer scrutiny of customers,

53
00:03:04,471 --> 00:03:07,621
the consequences could extend
beyond one individual.

54
00:03:07,661 --> 00:03:11,567
That is a possible channel of impact,
not a new restriction we are announcing.

55
00:03:11,607 --> 00:03:15,953
A political demand, a proposed law and
an enacted rule are different things.

56
00:03:17,293 --> 00:03:19,858
Third, governance and legal process.

57
00:03:19,898 --> 00:03:24,286
Reuters reports that shareholders filed
a proposed class action on Monday,

58
00:03:24,326 --> 00:03:26,200
alleging misleading disclosures.

59
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,770
Those accusations have not
been established by a court.

60
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:31,444
The filing adds another process to follow;

61
00:03:31,484 --> 00:03:34,882
it does not tell us what the
eventual outcome will be.

62
00:03:38,322 --> 00:03:41,992
At the November ninth regular-session
close, Nvidia was a hundred

63
00:03:42,032 --> 00:03:46,730
and seventy-eight dollars and sixty-seven
cents, down four point two seven percent.

64
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:50,824
Reuters put the day's market-value
decline at approximately a hundred

65
00:03:50,864 --> 00:03:52,426
and ninety billion dollars.

66
00:03:52,466 --> 00:03:55,610
That is a change in the market's
valuation of the shares.

67
00:03:55,650 --> 00:03:56,656
It is not a hundred

68
00:03:56,696 --> 00:04:00,347
and ninety billion dollars disappearing
from Nvidia's cash balance.

69
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:04,143
And the lawsuit was filed after the close.

70
00:04:04,183 --> 00:04:08,119
It cannot explain trading that had
already happened earlier that day.

71
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:10,546
Be careful with the wider decline as well.

72
00:04:10,586 --> 00:04:15,106
This story developed against
existing concerns about AI spending.

73
00:04:15,146 --> 00:04:18,420
We should not assign every earlier
price move to one cause simply

74
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:20,663
because a compelling
headline arrived later.

75
00:04:22,003 --> 00:04:24,101
The price tells you what investors paid.

76
00:04:24,141 --> 00:04:28,325
It does not, by itself, tell you whether
the next price is higher or lower, or

77
00:04:28,365 --> 00:04:30,437
whether the business offers good value.

78
00:04:34,677 --> 00:04:37,514
So put the headlines beside
the financial evidence.

79
00:04:37,554 --> 00:04:42,420
In its latest reported quarter, fiscal
twenty twenty-seven's second quarter,

80
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:46,551
Nvidia recorded ninety-six point
two billion dollars in revenue.

81
00:04:46,591 --> 00:04:49,079
Eighty-nine billion of that
came from data centres.

82
00:04:49,119 --> 00:04:52,140
Its reported gross margin
was seventy-five percent.

83
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:56,943
Those figures describe the quarter
already reported in August.

84
00:04:56,983 --> 00:04:58,502
They are not this month's earnings.

85
00:04:59,842 --> 00:05:03,042
For the third quarter,
management guided to a hundred

86
00:05:03,082 --> 00:05:06,955
and eight billion dollars of
revenue, plus or minus two percent.

87
00:05:06,995 --> 00:05:10,590
Its gross-margin outlook was
seventy-four percent, plus

88
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,770
or minus half a percentage point.

89
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:16,765
The revenue outlook assumed no
China data-centre compute revenue.

90
00:05:18,105 --> 00:05:19,676
That last point matters:

91
00:05:19,716 --> 00:05:24,779
do not casually add a large China
contribution to a forecast that explicitly

92
00:05:24,819 --> 00:05:25,585
excludes it.

93
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:30,773
But excluding those sales does not remove
every possible political, customer

94
00:05:30,813 --> 00:05:32,207
or reputational risk.

95
00:05:32,247 --> 00:05:34,021
These are company expectations.

96
00:05:34,061 --> 00:05:37,947
On November seventeenth, investors
get to compare them with results

97
00:05:37,987 --> 00:05:39,471
and hear the next outlook.

98
00:05:42,911 --> 00:05:47,096
The results are scheduled for around
nine twenty in the evening UK time,

99
00:05:47,136 --> 00:05:48,856
with the earnings call at ten.

100
00:05:48,896 --> 00:05:53,295
For the business, ask whether revenue
met guidance, whether margins held up,

101
00:05:53,335 --> 00:05:56,800
and what management says about
future demand and deliveries.

102
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:59,861
Listen for evidence of
changed customer behaviour,

103
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:03,289
rather than assuming either
resilience or cancellations.

104
00:06:04,629 --> 00:06:06,432
Then there is November eighteenth.

105
00:06:06,472 --> 00:06:10,850
Three House committee chairs requested
a closed-door briefing, with a response

106
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:13,739
or alternative date requested
by November eleventh.

107
00:06:13,779 --> 00:06:17,109
A requested appearance is not
the same as confirmed attendance.

108
00:06:17,149 --> 00:06:20,573
Their questions concern security
and the reported relationships.

109
00:06:20,613 --> 00:06:24,823
Those are different from whether a
quarterly sales figure beats expectations.

110
00:06:26,163 --> 00:06:29,378
A strong earnings report could
support confidence in demand.

111
00:06:29,418 --> 00:06:33,087
It would not complete the board's
investigation, settle the lawsuit

112
00:06:33,127 --> 00:06:35,246
or answer every congressional question.

113
00:06:36,586 --> 00:06:40,008
Trump has also said the FBI
is looking into the matter,

114
00:06:40,048 --> 00:06:44,351
and described Jensen telling him he
did not know the woman was a spy.

115
00:06:44,391 --> 00:06:47,503
That is Trump's account of
a private conversation.

116
00:06:47,543 --> 00:06:51,060
We should not present it as
independent FBI confirmation,

117
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,307
or a finding about what Jensen knew.

118
00:06:57,347 --> 00:06:59,981
Think in scenarios, not promises.

119
00:07:00,021 --> 00:07:04,493
In a constructive scenario, the
investigation provides credible clarity,

120
00:07:04,533 --> 00:07:06,122
leadership remains stable,

121
00:07:06,162 --> 00:07:09,945
and the operating results support
continuing customer demand.

122
00:07:09,985 --> 00:07:12,049
That could reduce uncertainty.

123
00:07:12,089 --> 00:07:15,047
It would not guarantee an
immediate share-price recovery.

124
00:07:16,387 --> 00:07:20,331
In a middle scenario, demand
holds up while the investigation

125
00:07:20,371 --> 00:07:22,421
and political scrutiny continue.

126
00:07:22,461 --> 00:07:27,030
A strong business can still trade under
a cloud of uncertainty for a long time.

127
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:32,968
In an adverse scenario, new findings
materially change the governance picture,

128
00:07:33,008 --> 00:07:36,714
policy becomes more restrictive,
or operating guidance weakens.

129
00:07:36,754 --> 00:07:39,829
Any of those would require
a fresh assessment.

130
00:07:39,869 --> 00:07:43,066
None should be stated as an
event that has already occurred.

131
00:07:43,106 --> 00:07:46,708
We are not assigning probabilities
or inventing price targets.

132
00:07:46,748 --> 00:07:50,911
We are identifying the evidence that
would make each scenario more plausible.

133
00:07:55,151 --> 00:07:58,318
Before making a decision,
ask four questions.

134
00:07:58,358 --> 00:08:01,275
What has actually been
confirmed since my last review?

135
00:08:01,315 --> 00:08:03,349
Has the earnings outlook changed?

136
00:08:03,389 --> 00:08:06,663
Has a political proposal
become an enforceable rule?

137
00:08:06,703 --> 00:08:10,428
And is my exposure small enough that
I can handle an uncertain outcome?

138
00:08:11,768 --> 00:08:15,861
Right now, the verified story is an
admission, an open investigation

139
00:08:15,901 --> 00:08:17,138
and growing scrutiny,

140
00:08:17,178 --> 00:08:21,270
alongside a very large operating
business awaiting its next results.

141
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:23,879
Treat the allegations seriously.

142
00:08:23,919 --> 00:08:25,545
Keep their attribution intact.

143
00:08:25,585 --> 00:08:28,887
And judge the business using
evidence as it arrives.

144
00:08:30,227 --> 00:08:34,570
Follow AI Finance Toolkit for more clear
explanations of the companies behind the

145
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:35,111
headlines.

146
00:08:35,151 --> 00:08:39,252
This is educational commentary, not a
personal recommendation to buy or sell.
